  {
    "id": "shahada",
    "title": "Shahada - Declaration of Faith",
    "image": "https://ik.imagekit.io/4zbzbdytp/imgi_21_topic_abrahamic_religions-24Ub5MbtndBYdeZHxSMfyV.webp?updatedAt=1781117902606",
    "emoji": "☪️",
    "category": "pillars_of_islam",
    "content": {
      "starter": "The Shahada says: \"There is no god but Allah, and Muhammad is His messenger.\" This is the most important sentence in Islam! When we say it, we tell everyone we believe in Allah and love His Prophet. It makes our heart light and happy!",
      "explorer": "The Shahada is the first pillar of Islam. It has two parts: first, believing that only Allah is God — no one else deserves worship. Second, believing that Prophet Muhammad ﷺ is Allah's final messenger. Saying the Shahada with sincerity makes you Muslim. It's not just words — it's a promise from your heart to follow Allah's guidance.",
      "thinker": "The Shahada is far more than a declaration — it's a complete worldview. The first part, \"La ilaha illallah,\" negates all false gods and affirms monotheism (Tawheed). The second part, \"Muhammadun rasulullah,\" establishes the prophetic authority of Muhammad ﷺ. Together, they form the foundation upon which all other Islamic practices are built. Understanding the Shahada means understanding the essence of submission to Allah."
    },
    "funFact": "Did you know? The Shahada is whispered into a newborn baby's ear and is also the last words many Muslims hope to say before they pass away!",
    "quiz": [
      {
        "q": "What does Shahada mean?",
        "options": [
          "Declaration of Faith",
