        "explanation": "Muslims give 2.5% (one-fortieth) of their savings as Zakat each year."
      },
      {
        "q": "What does the word 'Zakat' mean?",
        "options": [
          "Charity",
          "Purification",
          "Prayer"
        ],
        "correct": 1,
        "explanation": "Zakat means 'purification' — it purifies our wealth and our hearts."
      },
      {
        "q": "Who receives Zakat?",
        "options": [
          "Only family",
          "People in need",
          "Only the rich"
        ],
        "correct": 1,
        "explanation": "Zakat is given to people in need, including the poor, debtors, and travelers."
      }
