  {
    "id": "wudu",
    "title": "Wudu - Ablution",
    "image": "https://ik.imagekit.io/4zbzbdytp/imgi_11_topic_prayer_salah-AiQHjTprGERKrV6ZWGWS6N.webp?updatedAt=1781117901214",
    "emoji": "🚿",
    "category": "daily_practices",
    "content": {
      "starter": "Wudu is washing before prayer! We wash our hands, mouth, nose, face, arms, head, and feet with clean water. It makes us clean and ready to talk to Allah. Wudu also washes away our small sins — how cool is that!",
      "explorer": "Wudu is the ritual ablution Muslims perform before praying. It involves washing specific body parts in order: hands, mouth, nose, face, arms to elbows, wiping the head, and washing feet to ankles. Wudu is not just about physical cleanliness — it's also spiritual purification. Each step has benefits: washing the hands removes germs, rinsing the mouth keeps it clean, and washing the feet removes dirt from the road.",
      "thinker": "Wudu is a beautiful act that combines physical hygiene with spiritual purification. The Quran states: 'Indeed, Allah loves those who are constantly repenting and loves those who purify themselves' (Surah Al-Baqarah 2:222). The Prophet ﷺ said that when a Muslim performs wudu and washes their face, sins fall away with the water. When they wash their hands, sins fall from their hands. When they wash their feet, sins fall from their feet. Wudu is thus both a practical act of cleanliness and a spiritual ritual of renewal."
    },
    "funFact": "Did you know? When you perform wudu and wash each body part, your sins fall away with the water — it's like getting a fresh start!",
    "quiz": [
      {
        "q": "What do we perform before praying?",
        "options": [
          "Ghusl",
          "Wudu",
          "Tayammum"
        ],
        "correct": 1,
        "explanation": "We perform wudu (ablution) before praying to clean ourselves."
      },
      {
        "q": "How many steps are in wudu?",
        "options": [
          "3 steps",
          "7 steps",
          "10 steps"
        ],
        "correct": 1,
