    "emoji": "🧘",
    "category": "islamic_values",
    "content": {
      "starter": "Patience means waiting calmly and not getting upset when things are hard! When you're sick, or something goes wrong, or you have to wait — be patient! Allah loves patient people and will reward them!",
      "explorer": "Patience (Sabr) is one of the greatest virtues in Islam. The Quran says: 'Indeed, the patient will be given their reward without account' (Surah Az-Zumar 39:10). Sabr means staying calm during difficulties, resisting temptation, and being content with Allah's plan. The Prophet ﷺ compared patience to a precious gem — it's hard to find but incredibly valuable.",
      "thinker": "Patience (Sabr) is one of the most emphasized virtues in Islam. The Quran mentions it over 70 times. Sabr has three dimensions: patience in obeying Allah (perseverance), patience in avoiding sin (restraint), and patience during hardship (endurance). Allah says: 'And be patient, for indeed, Allah does not allow to be lost the reward of those who do good' (Surah Hud 11:115). The Prophet ﷺ said: 'How wonderful is the affair of the believer, for all his affairs are good, and this does not apply to anyone except the believer. If something good happens to him, he is grateful, and that is good for him. If something bad happens to him, he bears it with patience, and that is good for him.'"
    },
