      "starter": "Gratitude means saying 'thank you' to Allah for everything! For food, family, friends, health — everything! When we're thankful, Allah gives us more blessings. A grateful heart is a happy heart!",
      "explorer": "Gratitude (Shukr) means recognizing and appreciating Allah's blessings. The Quran says: 'If you are grateful, I will surely increase you' (Surah Ibrahim 14:7). Gratitude isn't just saying 'Alhamdulillah' — it's using Allah's blessings in ways that please Him. When we're grateful for health, we use it to do good. When we're grateful for wealth, we share it with others.",
      "thinker": "Gratitude (Shukr) is a comprehensive Islamic concept that goes beyond simple thankfulness. It has three dimensions: gratitude of the heart (recognizing blessings), gratitude of the tongue (verbal thanks and praise), and gratitude of the limbs (using blessings in obedience to Allah). The Quran warns against ingratitude: 'If you are ungrateful, indeed, my punishment is severe' (Surah Ibrahim 14:7). The Prophet ﷺ would pray at night until his feet would swell, and when asked why, he would say: 'Should I not be a grateful servant?' Gratitude transforms our perspective — even in hardship, a grateful person finds blessings to thank Allah for."
