        "explanation": "We perform wudu (ablution) to clean ourselves before praying."
      },
      {
        "q": "Which direction do Muslims face when praying?",
        "options": [
          "North",
          "The Kaaba in Mecca",
          "East"
        ],
        "correct": 1,
        "explanation": "Muslims face the Kaaba in Mecca, which is called the Qibla."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "zakat",
    "title": "Zakat - Charity",
    "image": "https://ik.imagekit.io/4zbzbdytp/imgi_45_zakat_overview-iB69C239XxvYzdfsgqWaNR.webp?updatedAt=1781117902141",
    "emoji": "💰",
    "category": "pillars_of_islam",
    "content": {
      "starter": "Zakat means sharing what we have with others! If we have extra money, we give a little bit to people who need it. It's like Allah is asking us to be kind and share. When we give, our hearts feel happy!",
      "explorer": "Zakat is the third pillar of Islam. It means giving 2.5% of your savings each year to those in need. It's not optional — it's an obligation for Muslims who have wealth above a certain amount. Zakat purifies our money and reminds us that everything belongs to Allah. It helps the poor, pays off debts, and strengthens the community.",
      "thinker": "Zakat is both a social and spiritual obligation. The word 'zakat' means 'purification' and 'growth' — by giving a portion of our wealth, we purify the remainder and grow spiritually. Allah says in the Quran that those who pay Zakat are helping to purify themselves (At-Tawbah 9:103). The fixed rate of 2.5% (one-fortieth) applies to savings held for one lunar year above the nisab threshold. This systematic approach to wealth redistribution was revolutionary and remains one of Islam's most powerful social justice mechanisms."
    },
    "funFact": "Did you know? The word 'Zakat' means 'purification' — when you give Zakat, your remaining money becomes blessed and pure!",
    "quiz": [
      {
        "q": "What percentage of savings is given as Zakat?",
        "options": [
          "1%",
          "2.5%",
          "10%"
        ],
