  {
    "id": "holy_books",
    "title": "Holy Books",
    "image": "https://ik.imagekit.io/4zbzbdytp/imgi_41_ramadan_quran-Q4vPHzY2VWydTXwzmZNchH.webp?updatedAt=1781117900610",
    "emoji": "📕",
    "category": "core_beliefs",
    "content": {
      "starter": "Allah sent holy books to guide people! The most important one for us is the Quran — Allah's final book, sent to Prophet Muhammad ﷺ. Before that, Allah sent the Torah to Musa, the Zabur to Dawud, and the Injil to Isa. The Quran is special because Allah promised to protect it!",
      "explorer": "Muslims believe that Allah revealed several holy books to guide humanity. The Tawrat (Torah) was given to Prophet Musa, the Zabur (Psalms) to Prophet Dawud, and the Injil (Gospel) to Prophet Isa. The Quran is the final and most complete revelation, sent to Prophet Muhammad ﷺ. We believe the earlier books were changed over time, but the Quran has been preserved exactly as Allah revealed it.",
      "thinker": "The belief in holy books (Kutub) is the third article of Islamic faith. Allah revealed guidance through various scriptures: the Sahifat to Ibrahim, the Tawrat to Musa, the Zabur to Dawud, the Injil to Isa, and the Quran to Muhammad ﷺ. While Muslims respect all these revelations, we believe the Quran is the final and preserved word of Allah. It was revealed over 23 years and has been memorized by millions of huffaz (memorizers) throughout history. The Quran is unique in that Allah Himself guaranteed its preservation: 'Indeed, it is We who sent down the Quran and indeed, We will be its guardian' (Surah Al-Hijr 15:9)."
    },
