      "starter": "Duas are prayers we say to Allah anytime! When we wake up, eat, go outside, or feel scared — we can talk to Allah. He always listens! There's a special dua for everything. It's like having a direct line to Allah!",
      "explorer": "Duas are personal prayers to Allah — conversations where we ask for help, guidance, forgiveness, or express gratitude. Unlike formal salah, duas can be made anytime in any language. The Prophet ﷺ taught us specific duas for waking up, eating, traveling, and more. Making dua shows our dependence on Allah and our trust in His help.",
      "thinker": "Duas (supplications) represent the direct relationship between a servant and Allah. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Dua is the essence of worship.' Islam teaches duas for every occasion — from waking up ('Alhamdulillahilladhi ahyana ba'da ma amatana wa ilayhin-nushur') to entering the mosque, before sleeping, and during times of distress. Allah says: 'Call upon Me; I will respond to you' (Surah Ghafir 40:60). This is a profound promise — the Creator of the universe invites us to speak with Him directly, without any intermediary."
