  {
    "id": "honesty",
    "title": "Honesty",
    "image": "https://ik.imagekit.io/4zbzbdytp/imgi_22_topic_shared_values-KgUz6j3XRCxAXqD4mpnH5G.webp?updatedAt=1781117903378",
    "emoji": "🤝",
    "category": "islamic_values",
    "content": {
      "starter": "Honesty means always telling the truth! Allah loves people who are honest. Even if telling the truth is hard, it's always the right thing to do. When we're honest, people trust us and Allah is pleased with us!",
      "explorer": "Honesty (Sidq) is one of the most important values in Islam. The Prophet ﷺ was known as 'Al-Amin' — the Trustworthy — because he always told the truth. Islam teaches us to be honest in our words, actions, and intentions. Lying is a major sin that can damage relationships and break trust. Being honest, even when it's difficult, earns Allah's love and the respect of others.",
      "thinker": "Honesty (Sidq) and trustworthiness (Amanah) are foundational Islamic virtues. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise.' Honesty is not merely about not lying — it encompasses sincerity in intentions, accuracy in reporting, and integrity in all dealings. Allah says in the Quran: 'O you who believe, fear Allah and be among the truthful' (Surah At-Tawbah 9:119). The concept extends to being honest with oneself, honest in worship, and honest in business dealings."
