      "starter": "Ramadan is the best month! It's when Allah sent the Quran. We fast from sunrise to sunset — no eating or drinking! At night, we pray, read Quran, and have iftar with family. Everyone is happy and kind during Ramadan!",
      "explorer": "Ramadan is the ninth month of the Islamic calendar and the holiest month for Muslims. The Quran was first revealed during Ramadan. Muslims fast from dawn to sunset, refraining from food, drink, and other physical needs. It's a time of increased prayer, charity, and Quran reading. Ramadan teaches self-discipline, empathy for the poor, and brings families and communities together.",
      "thinker": "Ramadan is the month in which the Quran was revealed as guidance for humanity (Surah Al-Baqarah 2:185). Fasting (Sawm) during Ramadan is the fourth pillar of Islam and serves multiple purposes: developing taqwa (God-consciousness), purifying the soul, building empathy for the less fortunate, and strengthening community bonds. The pre-dawn meal (Suhoor) and sunset meal (Iftar) create a spiritual rhythm throughout the month. The last 10 nights are especially sacred, as Laylat al-Qadr (the Night of Power) — described as 'better than a thousand months' — falls within them. Ramadan transforms communities: charity increases, tempers cool, and hearts soften."
    },
